## 2. Research Landscape

### Major Paradigms in Dynamic Community Detection

| Paradigm | Representative Methods | Strengths | Weaknesses |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| **Snapshot-based** | Static Louvain/Leiden per timestep | Simple, high quality per snapshot | O(n log²n) per snapshot, no temporal coherence |
| **Incremental/Frontier** | DynaMo, Dynamic Frontier, HIT-Leiden | Fast, maintains quality | Engineering-heavy, limited theoretical justification |
| **Streaming/Online** | TILES, iLCD, StreamComm | Single-pass, low memory | Sacrifices global quality, overlapping focus |
