## 11. Strongest Recommended Research Direction

### Primary: Incremental Surprise Optimization

**Title:** *"Beyond Modularity: Resolution-Limit-Free Incremental Community Detection via Surprise Optimization"*

**Core contributions:**
1. First formalization of incremental Surprise update rules under edge insertion/deletion
2. An incremental algorithm that maintains Surprise-optimal (or near-optimal) partitions without full recomputation
3. Theoretical analysis of Surprise sensitivity under k-edge perturbations
4. Comprehensive empirical comparison against modularity-based incremental methods (HIT-Leiden, DynaMo) showing superior community detection on graphs with multi-scale community structure

**Why this wins:**
- No competitor exists — complete first-mover advantage
- Addresses a fundamental limitation (resolution limit) that affects ALL existing methods
- Clear practical motivation: real social networks have multi-scale communities
- Differentiates cleanly from HIT-Leiden (which optimizes modularity)

### Fallback: Formal Locality Theory

If Surprise incremental optimization proves intractable, fall back to the formal locality analysis with the algorithm as corollary. This is harder mathematically but has strong publication potential even with partial results.

